-- ── THE ROOT CAUSE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- The sea is a 0.25-degree raster (public.sea_raster, 0046), scan-filled from Natural Earth 1:110m: no
-- Socotra at all, no Bangka, coasts straight for 60 nm. The pathfinder searched that raster and
-- straightened its course against it, and voyage.path_refusal judges the same line the same way, so every
-- course was legal water and was drawn on the chart's 1:10m coast (public/coast) straight over islands,
-- capes and peninsulas. The stored Hadibu to Kilwa lane was one straight line from the quay across Socotra.
-- Three further causes (0440 is one file for all of them, folded from the two drafts #734 and #736):
--   * a course's turn (a raster cell centre) on an island the raster cannot see: the refiner now searches
--     across the turn (src/lib/sea/refine.ts, the browser's course author and this generator alike);
--   * water the raster closes and the chart draws: CHARTED channels (below);
--   * a roadstead on drawn land, or in a pocket the open sea cannot reach: moved onto the water (below).
--
